16216	{"artifactId":"LLD-6a1315585c38c41c-s2","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-6a1315585c38c41c-s2-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-09T06:26:26.326Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The DEF's s2 requirements (FR001 card content with standalone flag and text-labelled badges, FR002 search/scope/needs-attention filter on the daemon's decision, FR003 counts over the whole selection) and ac1–ac6 are all designed.","evidence":"DEF.md:43-45 and :130-135. The LLD covers each one: §2.1 postconditions (six STAGE_ORDER columns; scope, search and needsAttentionOnly; total = cards.length + hiddenCount; badges labelled from DISPLAY_LABELS), §2.2 paging, k9 determinism, and textContent rendering (ac6). Nothing in the LLD builds a non-goal: details, the rollup and the narrow-pane layout are left to s3, s4 and s5. [files: docs/epics/e2-delivery-board-vs-code-goal-E202610086a131558/DEF.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every DEF decision assigned to S2 is designed or explicitly deferred.","evidence":"DEF.md:79 says: '\"Complete\" stays as the final stage's label; whether readers take it for validation success is tested in a usability session that the epics plan assigns to S2, outside this Define's acceptance criteria. [[c11]]'. The LLD cites c11 in §8 but no section plans, schedules or defers that usability session. The DEF review also proposed adding it as an S2 acceptance criterion (DEF.md:306). [files: docs/epics/e2-delivery-board-vs-code-goal-E202610086a131558/DEF.md]","action":"Add a short note to the LLD that keeps the 'Complete' label and either plans the usability check (who runs it, and what result would switch the label to 'Completion approved') or explicitly defers it, with the reason.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The host's dispatch builds the down-messages before it commits state, and s1's refresh path recovers from a throw by dispatching a failed refresh over the previous board.","evidence":"board-host.ts:106-111: `const next = reduceBoardState(state, event); const messages = boardDownMessages(next, DISPLAY_LABELS); state = next;`. board-host.ts:141-154 catches the throw, logs error(), and dispatches `{ ok: false, failure: { kind: 'read-failed', message } }`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"snapshot.items is sorted by id, so following snapshot order is deterministic even when timestamps are equal.","evidence":"snapshot.ts:150 builds the list with `const items = [...graph.items.keys()].sort(byText)...map(itemOf);`. types.ts:317 documents it with '/** Sorted by id. */'. [files: src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts, src/workflow/delivery/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An overridden review keeps effectiveVerdict 'block' with blocking false, which is what the edge case 'Review blocked with tone neutral' relies on.","evidence":"gate.ts:190: `const blocking = review.effectiveVerdict === 'block' && record.approval.state !== 'approved' && review.override === null;`. An override does not change effectiveVerdict (gate.ts:112-123), so the edge-case row matches the data. [files: src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"STAGE_ORDER and DISPLAY_LABELS (sc4) already exist and have the shape the model reuses: six stages in order, plus approval, reviewVerdict, attention, notice and taskResult tables.","evidence":"labels.ts:34-41 defines STAGE_ORDER with the six stages in order. labels.ts:43-89 defines DISPLAY_LABELS with stage, attention, notice, taskResult, approval and reviewVerdict ('block' -> 'Review blocked', 'validation-conflict' -> 'Validation conflict'). [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The fields the plugin-side Pick gains (standalone, sourceIds, validation, conflict, correctsRef) already exist on the daemon's DeliveryItem, so the addition is purely a mirror change.","evidence":"types.ts:285-308 declares DeliveryItem with standalone, sourceIds, validation (ItemGates['validation'] | null), conflict and correctsRef. delivery-contract.ts:59-60 currently picks 'id' | 'kind' | 'title' | 'parentId' | 'childIds' | 'stage' | 'evidence' | 'needsAttention' | 'attentionReasons' | 'notices'. [files: src/workflow/delivery/types.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The validation badge can be built from validation.failed and the unrecorded tasks ('Validation failed when validation.failed > 0 … otherwise Passed').","evidence":"gate.ts:349 counts tasks only: `failed: validation.tasks.filter(t => t.result === 'failed').length`. A failed story-level result is kept separately in storyLevelResult (gate.ts:301, snapshot.ts:140), but it still raises attention: gate.ts:341 `... || validation.storyLevelResult === 'failed') reasons.add('validation-failed')`, and it can set conflict (types.ts:217). When a story's tasks all passed but its story-level result failed, the rule as written shows a 'Passed' validation badge next to a 'Validation failed' attention badge. That is a contradictory signal, and it departs from the daemon's own fact (k2). [files: src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts, src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts]","action":"Change the validation-badge rule to read storyLevelResult as well: 'Validation failed' when validation.failed > 0 or storyLevelResult === 'failed', and 'Unrecorded' when an unrecorded task or storyLevelResult === 'unrecorded'. Add the case to the badge fixture.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The call-site inventory for replacing 'items' with 'board' and adding paging to boardDownMessages is complete (board-protocol.ts, board-state.ts, board-host.ts).","evidence":"Existing s1 tests read the 'items' message directly and call the two-argument signature: board-state.test.ts:43-44, :82-87 (`boardDownMessages(state, DISPLAY_LABELS)...find(p => p.type === 'items')`, including the unknown-stage label test), and board-host.test.ts:79-80, :120, :240-244 (the webview test delivers `{ type: 'items', ... }`). Removing the message breaks these tests. Neither §3.1's call sites nor §6 says whether to rewrite or retire them, or which 'board' tests replace their coverage. One example is the s1 test that an unlabelled stage shows its raw id; under s2 that item is dropped instead. The BoardDownMessage 'items' variant itself is also not said to be removed or kept. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-state.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-host.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts]","action":"List board-state.test.ts and board-host.test.ts as change sites. Say which s1 assertions move to 'board' messages and which are retired (with the unknown-stage behaviour change made explicit). State whether the 'items' variant stays in BoardDownMessage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"parseBoardUpMessage can take the show-more variant the same way as its existing validated cases, and the host's existing malformed-message path logs the rejection through warn().","evidence":"board-protocol.ts:82-110 is a switch that returns null for any mistyped field. board-host.ts:190-195 does `if (msg === null) { deps.logger.warn('delivery board: ignored a malformed webview message'); return; }`. A `case 'show-more'` that checks the stage against STAGE_ORDER fits this pattern. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored shape changes: paging stays in host memory only, the DeliveryItemView change is additive, and the snapshot stays at schemaVersion 1.","evidence":"The host state is in-memory: board-host.ts:95-97 holds `let state ... let nextSeq` and reset() at :173-178 discards it. The client accepts only schemaVersion 1 (delivery-client.ts:115). The Pick in delivery-contract.ts:59-60 only gains existing daemon fields. Nothing is written to the store. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s2 changes the s1-owned sc3 only through a pending, additive amendment, and the boardDownMessages signature change does not touch any part of the HLD's sc2 contract.","evidence":".insrc/artifacts/AMD-6a1315585c38c41c-2.json has `\"type\": \"sharedContract.fieldAdd\", \"contractId\": \"sc3\", \"breaking\": false`, adds `{ readonly type: 'show-more'; readonly stage: DeliveryStage }`, and has status 'pending'. The HLD's sc2 sketch (HLD.md:120-128) declares BoardState and BoardSelection but not boardDownMessages, and BoardSelection is not extended. That was alternative a3, which the LLD rejected. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-6a1315585c38c41c-2.json, docs/epics/e2-delivery-board-vs-code-goal-E202610086a131558/HLD.md]","action":"The amendment must be approved before the build.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"An item with an unknown stage is detected and the host logs one warn() per refresh naming the stage id and its count.","evidence":"buildBoardViewModel is specified as pure, and BoardViewModel (HLD.md:249-254) has no field that reports dropped stages, so the host cannot learn which stages were dropped or how many. boardDownMessages also runs on every dispatch and every post(): board-host.ts:102 on 'ready', :108 on every selection change and refresh event. A log placed there would fire on every search keystroke, not once per refresh. The statement 'counts still agree' holds, but the detection and logging seam is not designed. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, docs/epics/e2-delivery-board-vs-code-goal-E202610086a131558/HLD.md]","action":"Specify the seam, for example a separate pure helper `unknownStages(snapshot): ReadonlyMap<string, number>` that the host calls only when a 'snapshot-arrived' event is applied. Add a test that asserts exactly one warn() per refresh.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A throw while building the board model is recovered by s1's existing path, which ends the refresh as failed over the previous board.","evidence":"Recovery exists only in refresh() (board-host.ts:141-154). handle() calls dispatch() without try/catch for set-scope, set-search, set-attention and the rest (board-host.ts:157-171), and the new show-more uses the same path. post() on 'ready' (board-host.ts:101-103) also has no catch. The client checks only that items, rootIds and notices are lists (delivery-client.ts:117-119). Under the LLD's own matching rule, an item whose sourceIds or title is malformed renders fine with an empty search (because the search is trimmed to empty and nothing is read), passes the refresh, and then throws on the first set-search. That exception escapes from the webview onMessage handler with no state recovery and no stated user impact. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts]","action":"State the handling for a throw during a selection change, show-more or ready: for example, wrap dispatch in handle() and post() so that state is not committed, the error is logged, and the status is marked failed. Add a host test that uses a malformed sourceIds and a non-empty search.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1–ac6 maps to a named test, and the fixtures that the integration tests rely on already exist (a fake channel, and a runScript fake DOM whose innerHTML throws).","evidence":"LLD §6 maps ac1–ac5 to board-model.test.ts tests (ac4 also to a board-host.test.ts paging test) and ac6 to a board-host.test.ts literal-text test. The fixture exists: board-host.test.ts:203-214 says '/** A minimal DOM the script runs against: elements record textContent and children, and innerHTML throws. */' with `Object.defineProperty(e, 'innerHTML', { set() { throw ... } })`. board-state.test.ts already casts snapshots through unknown. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-host.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-state.test.ts]","action":"None for the acceptance criteria. The missing error-path tests are raised under error-paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":5,"low":10,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-09T06:26:26.326Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"coverage-of-intent.2":{"findingId":"coverage-of-intent.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: §2.1 keeps 'Complete' and defers the usability check to E2's usability session after s5, with the reason and the one-line label change that a misreading would trigger.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T06:30:37.169Z"},"new-versus-reuse.3":{"findingId":"new-versus-reuse.3","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: the validation badge now reads storyLevelResult too (failed -> Validation failed, unrecorded -> Unrecorded), and the fixture gains a story whose tasks passed but whose story-level result failed.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T06:30:37.171Z"},"change-sites.1":{"findingId":"change-sites.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: §3.1 lists board-state.test.ts and board-host.test.ts as change sites, says which s1 assertions move to 'board' and which one is retired (the unknown-stage raw id), and §2.3 keeps the 'items' variant in the type but unsent.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T06:30:37.172Z"},"error-paths.1":{"findingId":"error-paths.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: a pure unknownStages(snapshot) helper (§2.5) that the host calls only when a refresh applies a snapshot, logging one warn() per refresh, with a board-host test.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T06:30:37.173Z"},"error-paths.2":{"findingId":"error-paths.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: §2.3 states that every derive path (refresh, selection change, show-more, ready) keeps state only when rendering succeeds and logs through error() otherwise; §5 and a board-host test cover a malformed sourceIds hit by a search.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-09T06:30:37.174Z"}}}}}}
